OBSERVED FAILING FIRST against the unfixed code (0.74.0 + the test only), all 3 cases:
· the registry router answered an unlisted Host with 404 and its design listing ("This server's registry root holds no designs"), because no Host check ran before routing;
· the single-design server answered 403 with NO content type, rmcp's "Forbidden: Host header is not allowed", naming no flag;
· the named-host case passed its allowed paths and failed on the same opaque refusal.
With host_gate in front of serve_http and rmcp's check disabled, all 3 pass, and the 7 unit tests pass. Regression, all passing locally: tools/test_shared_sessions.py (the existing allowlist test, including 403-with-"Host" and loopback not locked out), test_degraded_server.py, refusal_speaks.py, test_export_to_reaches_the_daemon.py, test_shared_attach_from_another_folder.py, toolsnap.py, smoke_mcp.py; cargo clippy -p reflow2-mcp --all-targets -D warnings; cargo fmt --check.
